Field-major .odb table blocks, carried against the pinned OpenROAD.

NOT UPSTREAMED. Retires when a //:bump lands on an upstream that carries
the change.

What it does. An opted-in dbTable writes its pages in blocks whose bytes
are permuted field-major: byte j of every record, then byte j + 1. The same
bytes, in a different order, so no object id moves, no free-list order
changes, and no dbSet iteration order shifts -- which is what the DEF
equality gate in study/soa/roundtrip_gate.sh checks. Records are produced
by the type's existing operator<<, so no per-type serializer exists; that
was the condition the whole idea was conditional on.

How a table opts in. One line in its header:

    static constexpr bool kFieldMajorTable = true;

_dbITerm and _dbBox do here; _dbSBox inherits it from _dbBox, which is
intended for these two and a trap for any future derived slot type. A
per-type member rather than a trait specialization on purpose: dbTable<T>
is instantiated wherever the serialization happens, and a specialization
declared in T's own header need not be visible there, so writer and reader
could disagree -- a silently corrupt file.

Compatibility. kSchemaFieldMajorBlocks gates the read. Files older than it
take the per-slot path unchanged: simple, and deliberately not made fast,
since it runs only on files written before the bump.

Measured, seven public ORFS designs, both gates passing on all of them:
compressed artifact 1.10x-2.72x smaller (1.53x aggregate), uncompressed
0.4%-1.5% smaller, read time +8%, peak RSS +0.2%, write time unchanged.

Known limit. Block size is bounded by slots and by an estimate of bytes
that uses sizeof(T), so it does not bind for types whose records carry a
heap payload -- a net and its wire. Opting every table in reaches 2.45x on
the artifact but costs 7.1x read time and 2.3x peak RSS on
nangate45/ariane133. Slot-granular blocks that straddle pages would fix
that; until then the opt-in list is the three small-record tables.

Also included as study scaffolding, not part of any proposal: the
SoaLayoutFacts and SoaDumpTable probe targets in src/odb/src/db/BUILD.

